   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Turn It Out segued directly into Uncle Junior in the second slot of the reviewer's setlist [2]\n- Do The T? flowed into Too Much, according to the reviewer's list [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soullive-SMPeir-8-12-10-T08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soullive2010-08-12.soullive-santamonica8-12-10** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 10 songs; 76 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soullive2010-08-12.soullive-santamonica8-12-10**: taped by Pat Myers; transferred by Pat Myers; source: Neumann u89i-v3 +mono Sbd Feed-r4 [1]. Also: The reviewer identifies this recording as a matrix mix of the Santa Monica show [2]",
